Argus
=====

An MCP server that gives coding agents reliable browser control via
CDP.  Agents navigate, interact, take screenshots, inspect the DOM,
intercept network traffic, and collect diagnostic evidence — all
through composable MCP tools.

通过 CDP 让 coding agent 可靠操控浏览器的 MCP server。导航、交互、截图、
DOM 检查、网络拦截、诊断证据采集，全部通过可组合的 MCP 工具完成。


Features
--------

  * 48 MCP tools across 5 toolsets (default, core, diagnose, debug, full)
  * Single Go binary, no runtime dependencies
  * Persistent CDP connection pool with health check and reconnect
  * Flight recorder: ring buffer captures actions and browser events
  * Action results carry incremental evidence (console errors, failed
    requests, navigations) — agents see what each action actually did
  * Stable snapshot refs: snapshot/look return snapshot_id; click/fill
    accept snapshot=<id> for stale-reference detection
  * diff_snapshot reports added/removed/recreated/changed elements
  * start_recording/stop_recording: record a human session, replay it
    as batch_actions
  * Timeline query, diagnose, and trace export with redaction
  * URL scheme allowlist, cookie/secret redaction, upload path canonicalization
  * macOS, Linux, and Windows Chrome discovery


Build
-----

    go build -o argus .


Quick start
-----------

  1. Configure your MCP client (e.g. Claude Code):

       {
         "mcpServers": {
           "argus": {
             "command": "/path/to/argus",
             "args": ["--toolsets=default"]
           }
         }
       }

  2. Call the configure tool to set a target URL:

       {"url": "http://localhost:3000"}

  3. Use tools: navigate, snapshot, click, fill, screenshot, find, etc.


Toolsets
--------

`--toolsets` controls which tools are exposed to the MCP client.
The `default` loop (14 tools: navigate, eval, click, fill, snapshot, look,
screenshot, find, get_element, wait_for, exists, configure, status,
tool_summary) is always enabled — named sets add on top of it.

    default              compact agent loop only (no extra sets)
    core                 + tabs, scroll, type, emulate, batch_actions,
                           diff_snapshot, recording
    diagnose             + network, trace, console, intercept, PDF
    debug                + debugger + source mapping
    full                 all tools, incl. deprecated aliases/escape hatches

Example: `--toolsets=core,diagnose` exposes default + core + diagnose.
Can also be set via ARGUS_TOOLSETS environment variable.


Snapshots and batch actions
---------------------------

snapshot/look store the interactive-element map and return a
snapshot_id.  Pass it to click/fill as {"snapshot": "snap_0001"} to get
stale-reference errors instead of silently clicking a re-rendered node.

diff_snapshot compares the current page to a stored snapshot:
added/removed/recreated/changed elements, URL change, plus evidence
collected since that snapshot.

batch_actions steps: click, fill, type, wait_for, hover, scroll,
navigate, assert (element/text/url check), extract (name=value pulled
from an element into {{name}} variables usable by later steps), and an
optional flag per step to skip failures instead of aborting.

start_recording injects a listener that captures human clicks/fills/keys
across navigations; stop_recording returns steps in batch_actions format
(replay verbatim) and saves them under ~/.local/share/argus/recordings/.


Window focus
------------

By default Argus never covers your screen: Chrome launches hidden in the
background and tabs are created/selected without raising the window.
Everything still works — screenshot, snapshot, click, evaluate do not
require the window to be visible.

Pass `--focus` (or `ARGUS_FOCUS=true`, or `{"focus": true}` via the
configure tool) to opt into foreground behavior: Chrome activates on
launch and new/selected tabs are raised to the front.


Flight recorder
---------------

Argus continuously captures browser events and agent actions:

  * timeline    query recent console/exception/log events and actions
  * diagnose    one-shot page diagnostics (console errors + failed actions)
  * export_trace    export JSON evidence bundle (actions + events + status)

All trace output is redacted (JWT, Bearer tokens, passwords, API keys,
private keys, etc.).


Environment variables
---------------------

    ARGUS_CDP_PORT          9224                              Chrome CDP port
    ARGUS_PROFILE_DIR       ~/.config/argus/chrome-profile    Chrome profile
    ARGUS_USE_USER_PROFILE  false                             use real profile
    ARGUS_CHROME_BINARY     auto-detect                       Chrome binary path
    ARGUS_LOG               info                              log level
    ARGUS_TOOLSETS          default                           exposed toolsets
    ARGUS_URL               (none)                            initial target URL
    ARGUS_ATTACH            false                             attach, don't launch
    ARGUS_PROFILE           isolated                          isolated|user
    ARGUS_FOCUS             false                             foreground Chrome


Development
-----------

    gofmt -d *.go              format check
    go vet ./...              static analysis
    go test ./...             unit tests
    go test -race ./...       race detector
    go test -tags=integration ./...    Chrome integration tests


